# Cold-start Wake-on-LAN targets for `deploy/proxmox.sh wake-lab --ip-address 172.16.0.99`.
# The QDevice host sends the packets (it stays on); hosts are woken IN ORDER and each must
# answer on <port> before the next one is woken.
#
# Format: <name> <MAC> <ip> <port>
#   1. TrueNAS first (NFS :2049) — PVE mounts the HA export at boot.
#   2. Entry PVE node next (API :8006) — it hosts the LAN router guest.
#   3. Remaining PVE nodes (API :8006) — pve-001 alone holds 2/5 votes, so no guest (router
#      included) starts until peers join; its post-startup-proc only wakes them after a 120 s
#      quorum wait, so list them here.
#
# MACs: PVE nodes — `pvenode config get --property wakeonlan` (set in setup step 3);
#       TrueNAS — Network → Interfaces (BIOS/NIC WoL must be enabled).
# Override the file with PAPITA_WOL_MACS_FILE; tune PAPITA_WOL_WAIT_SEC (default 600) and
# PAPITA_WOL_BROADCAST (default 255.255.255.255).
#
# truenas  aa:bb:cc:dd:ee:00  172.16.0.100  2049
# pve-001  aa:bb:cc:dd:ee:01  172.16.0.101  8006
# pve-002  aa:bb:cc:dd:ee:02  172.16.0.102  8006
# pve-003  aa:bb:cc:dd:ee:03  172.16.0.103  8006
# pve-004  aa:bb:cc:dd:ee:04  172.16.0.104  8006
